#: src/app/map-editor/messages.ts:1171
msgid "mapEditor.help.contourTransform"
msgstr "Move or resize the measured contour profile. Relief is cut above its selected contour plane; an inland lake is filled to its waterline and its measured depths move to the new rim. Attached trees, stones and decorations keep their native appearance and size. This does not recover hidden original ground. Complete finite stone sources move with their boulders; complete ore zones retain their exact quantities when moved or resized. Enable connected courses to move or resize complete river groups with the measured relief, using the native river carver. Courses keep their saved order and fixed map erasures. Without this option, relief crossed by a flowing river is refused rather than moving the river implicitly; exact flowing water bodies still support whole-tile moves onto matching terrain. Other props, roads and authored features stay protected."

